      "bench_punchline_a": "In the ",
      "bench_punchline_b": ", one millilitre stands ",
      "bench_punchline_c": " mm tall — about ",
      "bench_punchline_d": "× what the same millilitre manages in a 250 mL beaker, where it is a ",
      "bench_punchline_e": " mm film you could not see, let alone read. That is the entire reason you titrate from a burette and not out of a beaker.",
      "bore_explains_tolerance": "A tolerance is not an arbitrary number stamped on the glass — it follows from how wide the vessel is where you read it. The blue slice in each vessel below is one millilitre, drawn to scale against that vessel's real bore.",
