      "moon_model_boundary": "The 12° phase and 1.5° latitude windows are illustrative teaching thresholds—not eclipse predictions. The model uses a 29.53059-day mean synodic month and 5.145° inclination, but omits changing distance and apparent size, orbital eccentricity, shadow-cone dimensions, node precession, observer location, and atmosphere. It cannot predict an eclipse date, type, path, or visibility.",
