      "key_debate_did_bats_evolve_flight_firs": "Key debate: Did bats evolve flight first, then echolocation? Or echolocation first, then flight? The Onychonycteris fossil suggests flight came first — but the question remains open.",
      "key_formulas_sound_physics_reference": "Key Formulas — Sound Physics Reference",
      "key_insight_bat_wings_are_essentially_": "Key insight: Bat wings are essentially hands with webbing. Each \"finger\" can be controlled independently, giving bats unparalleled maneuverability — essential for catching insects in mid-air using echolocation.",
